    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "f5e44ac30c8b91a92f672983b1055f82",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"muon-decay-and-three-body-phase-space\">Muon decay and three-body phase space</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/weak_decays.py\">W and top decays</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generate <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\mu^-\\to e^-\\bar\\nu_e\\nu_\\mu||)</marimo-tex> with the embedded Standard Model charged-current vertices. The existing W propagator supplies its complete unitary-gauge numerator, including the longitudinal term. Shared particle spin sums average the muon spin and sum all final spins.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">First compare the full squared amplitude with the <a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/EW/Tree/Mu-ElAnelNmu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">FeynCalc reference</a>, then derive the Fermi limit. The shared <code>Kinematics.three_body_phase_space</code> supplies the Dalitz measure, independently checked by a recursive two-body derivation. Symbolica integrates the resulting spectrum and finite-mass correction.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Write <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(M=m_\\mu||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(m=m_e||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(s=(p_e+p_{\\bar\\nu_e})^2||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t=(p_e+p_{\\nu_\\mu})^2||)</marimo-tex>. Both neutrinos are massless. The coupling convention is <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(e^4=32G_F^2m_W^4\\sin^4\\theta_W||)</marimo-tex>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
